+  _-Int_      hook(INT.sub)
+  _andBool_   hook(BOOL.and)
+  _>=Int_     hook(INT.ge)
+  _==Int_     hook(INT.eq)
+  _%Int_      hook(INT.tmod)
+  _+Int_      hook(INT.add)
+  _/Int_      hook(INT.tdiv)
+
+Frozen supplied semantics:
+  pyMod(I1,I2) => ((I1 %Int I2) +Int I2) %Int I2
+
+The candidate definitions are respectively Lean subtraction, Boolean &&,
+decidable integer >= and equality, Int.tmod, integer addition, Int.tdiv, and
+the exact nested tmod pyMod equation. SortInt is the generated alias Int and
+SortBool is Bool. The target only uses /Int and %Int with divisor 2; K makes
+these hooks undefined at divisor zero, so the candidate's total values at zero
+are outside every bound obligation and do not replace defined K behavior.
+
+Candidate triAt implements the frozen summary domain:
+  triAt(0)=1
+  triAt(1)=3
+  even i>=2: 1+i/2
+  odd i>=3: with k=(i+1)/2, k*(k+2)
+
+The odd closed form satisfies the source recurrence
+triAt(i-1)+triAt(i-2)+1+(i+1)/2 for odd i>=3. Values outside the nonnegative
+rule coverage are an arbitrary total extension and are not used by either
+obligation.
+
